Types of AI models used in Microsoft Online Services:
1. AI models hosted and operated by Microsoft
2. AI independent processors
3. AI Subprocessors

AI Models hosted and operated by Microsoft:
1. Certain AI models used in Microsoft Online Services are hosted on Azure and provided to customers directly by Microsoft (such as Azure OpenAI or Black Forest Labs FLUX).
2. evaluated and deeply integration in MS products
3. under microsoft Data protection addendum (DPA)
4. Data does not leave MS

AI Independent Processor:
1. An AI independent processor is a third-party AI provider that processes data under its own data processing commitments, privacy, compliance, and enterprise terms.
2. Data processing occurs outside MS

AI Subprocessor:
1. An AI Subprocessor is a third-party AI provider that handles data on Microsoft's behalf
2. When used, an AI Subprocessor handles data to deliver the specific services and functionalities Microsoft has engaged them to provide.


